=== Tolerant diagonal board — known-key garble grade ===
control       : P1030684 (published key), 120 letters
crib          : first 27 letters of the true plaintext, offset 0
true shell    : UKW B / Greek gamma / IV-III-VIII / rings AACU / pos VYAA

A tolerant board drops up to `t` menu edges that contradict the rest of the board,
on the hypothesis that a dropped edge is a mis-transcribed ciphertext letter.
tolerance 0 is the historical board exactly.

SENSITIVITY — does the true setting survive its own garbled ciphertext?
  garbled  tolerance=0        tolerance=g       plugs forced (correct/total)
        0  KEPT KEPT 25/25
        1  LOST KEPT 25/25
           corrupted positions [13]

SPECIFICITY — what does tolerance cost in surviving wrong settings?
Sampling 26³ window positions at the true shell on the CLEAN ciphertext.
  tolerance   survivors/17576    inflation vs exact
          0                1    1.0x
          1                1    1.0x

Read both columns together. Sensitivity without specificity is a ghost factory;
the inflation factor is what the crib-free escalator has to pay for, and it only
pays if a ghost still lands below the random-setting noise floor.
